<title>USA: FSA qualifies 11 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 11 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 11 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Deep River, Conn., $4.8 million general obligation bonds.  </p>
<p>--Mount Pleasant Community School District, Iowa, $4.53 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Panorama Community School District, Iowa, $5.495 million school GOs.</p>
<p>--Auburn, Mass., $2.51 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hancock Public Schools, Mich., $8.485 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Hibbing Independent School District No 701, Minn., $2.2 million GOs.</p>
<p>--South River, N.J., $3.475 million improvement GOs.</p>
<p>--Averill Park Central School District, N.Y., $12.5 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Irvington, N.Y., $1.239 million improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Malverne, N.Y., $1.497 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Metro, Ore., $28.8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Kathie O'Donnell, 212-859-1650</p>
